   208→### Anti-Patterns to Avoid
   209→- **Updating DOM on every frame during fast playback:** Use requestAnimationFrame throttling or batch updates to prevent performance issues
   210→- **Inline styles for highlighting:** Use CSS classes to enable transitions and maintain separation of concerns
   211→- **Creating new DOM nodes on every update:** Update textContent/classList only; create structure once
   212→- **Global querySelector every update:** Cache element references in view constructors
   213→- **Synchronous rendering blocking animation loop:** Keep render functions lightweight (<16ms)
   214→
   215→## Don't Hand-Roll
   216→
   217→| Problem | Don't Build | Use Instead | Why |
   218→|---------|-------------|-------------|-----|
   219→| Layout system | Custom positioning logic | CSS Grid + Flexbox | Native, responsive, accessible, well-tested |
   220→| State management | Custom pub/sub | CustomEvent on window | Already implemented, browser-optimized |
   221→| Value formatting | String concatenation | toLocaleString(), Intl.NumberFormat | Handles edge cases, i18n-ready |
   222→| Accessibility | Manual focus management | Native HTML elements + ARIA | Screen reader compatibility out-of-box |
   223→| Responsive design | JS resize listeners | CSS media queries | Declarative, performant, maintainable |
   224→| Animation timing | setTimeout loops | CSS transitions + requestAnimationFrame | GPU-accelerated, respects prefers-reduced-motion |
   225→
   226→**Key insight:** Browser APIs have evolved to handle common UI patterns efficiently. Custom solutions add maintenance burden and often miss edge cases (accessibility, internationalization, reduced motion preferences).
   227→
   228→## Common Pitfalls
   229→
   230→### Pitfall 1: Excessive DOM Updates During Playback
   231→**What goes wrong:** Updating all 32 register cells + 5 pipeline stages on every frame (2-4 FPS) causes jank
   232→**Why it happens:** Naive implementation updates entire view even when only 1-2 registers changed
   233→**How to avoid:** Check cpuState.changedRegisters and only update elements that actually changed
   234→**Warning signs:** Animation feels sluggish, CPU profiler shows high "Recalculate Style" time
   235→
   236→### Pitfall 2: Layout Thrashing (Read-Write-Read Pattern)
   237→**What goes wrong:** Reading offsetHeight/clientWidth after DOM writes forces synchronous reflow
   238→**Why it happens:** Measuring elements to position tooltips or calculate sizes
   239→**How to avoid:** Batch all reads before writes, or use ResizeObserver for async measurement
   240→**Warning signs:** Chrome DevTools shows "Forced reflow" warnings
   241→
   242→### Pitfall 3: Inaccessible Dynamic Content
   243→**What goes wrong:** Screen readers don't announce register value changes or pipeline stage transitions
   244→**Why it happens:** Forgetting ARIA live regions for dynamic content
   245→**How to avoid:** Use aria-live="polite" on register/cycle counter containers
   246→**Warning signs:** Testing with VoiceOver/NVDA reveals no feedback during animation
   247→
   248→### Pitfall 4: Non-Monospace Font Alignment Issues
   249→**What goes wrong:** Hex values like 0x0000000A and 0xFFFFFFFF have different widths, causing layout shift
   250→**Why it happens:** Using proportional font for numeric data
   251→**How to avoid:** Set font-family: var(--font-mono) and font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums on value displays
   252→**Warning signs:** Register grid column widths jump during value updates
   253→
   254→### Pitfall 5: Missing Responsive Breakpoints
   255→**What goes wrong:** Two-column layout becomes unusable on mobile/tablet
   256→**Why it happens:** Assuming desktop viewport
   257→**How to avoid:** Test at 320px, 768px, 1024px breakpoints; use CSS Grid auto-fit/minmax
   258→**Warning signs:** Horizontal scroll on mobile, text overflow, tiny touch targets
   259→
   260→### Pitfall 6: Performance Degradation with Template Cloning
   261→**What goes wrong:** Cloning &lt;template&gt; nodes 32 times per frame update is slower than expected
   262→**Why it happens:** MDN 2026 research shows DocumentFragment performance is "often overstated"
   263→**How to avoid:** Create DOM structure once, update textContent/classList only on subsequent frames
   264→**Warning signs:** Profiler shows significant time in cloneNode()
